{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1278","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Cards"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the following experiment. You have a deck of $$$m$$$ cards, and exactly one card is a joker. $$$n$$$ times, you do the following: shuffle the deck, take the top card of the deck, look at it and return it into the deck."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$x$$$ be the number of times you have taken the joker out of the deck during this experiment. Assuming that every time you shuffle the deck, all $$$m!$$$ possible permutations of cards are equiprobable, what is the expected value of $$$x^k$$$? Print the answer modulo $$$998244353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\lt 998244353$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le 5000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the expected value of $$$x^k$$$, taken modulo $$$998244353$$$ (the answer can always be represented as an irreducible fraction $$$\\frac{a}{b}$$$, where $